findings

  FINDING 399 access units over 5.00 s at 50.4 Mbps, 66.5 datagrams per unit of 1187 bytes mean
  FINDING complete-interval p50 0.177 ms, p99 104.464 ms, max 151.126 ms; first-datagram interval p99 68.289 ms, which separates a unit that starts late from one that finishes badly
  FINDING 64 crossings of two source periods and 60 stall clusters counted, which over 4.90 s is 784.2 and 735.2 a minute - the counts are what this window supports and the rates are what it can be compared on
  FINDING stall gaps p50 81.1 ms and p95 105.3 ms: a tight distribution indicts a timer - a scan, a beacon, a power-save cycle - and a broad one indicts contention, and the two need different actions

what must not be zero

  PASS  access units completed                   399
        the population under every zero in this arm. A probe that completed no access unit measured nothing, and zero datagrams lost out of zero sent is the most common way an instrument in this project has lied
  PASS  datagrams accounted for                  26830
        the population under the loss figure: datagrams the sequence machine accepted plus the gaps it saw. A loss ratio over nothing is not a small loss
  PASS  the radio said what it was               2
        a run whose conditions were not recorded cannot be compared with any other run, which is what happened to thirteen arms of the A8 sweep. This decides whether the run is comparable and never whether the link is good - the radio tier is barred from that, because -48 dBm at 1200 Mbps produced concealment from 0.196 to 7.442 per cent across ten arms
  PASS  the injected loss reached the path       284
        the relay was told to drop datagrams, and an arm that shows none of it is a fault that never reached the traffic rather than a link that survived one. This is the companion to the clean arm's zero: without an arm where it comes out the other way, that zero is unfalsifiable
  PASS  the probe saw the bunching               60
        the relay holds every datagram for the length of a stall and then releases them together, which is bunching and not loss, and crates/link-metrics counts it as a stall followed by units arriving early. A control arm whose held datagrams produced no cluster would mean the instrument cannot see what was done to it, which is the one thing a clean arm's silence cannot establish

what must be zero

  PASS  the channel held still                   0 over 2 conditions_reads
        the association is read before the probe and after it, and a channel or width that moved between the two means one report describes two links. Signal is deliberately not part of it: two reads seconds apart differ by a decibel or two on a link nobody touched, and a criterion that fires on that refuses every run
  PASS  the traffic was video shaped             0 over 399 access_units_delivered
        this product hands a whole access unit to the kernel at once, some tens of datagrams with no gap between them, and the burst is the part a link fails at. An access unit that would have fitted in one datagram is a probe pointed at traffic this link is never asked to carry, and every number beside it would then be about the wrong stream while looking reasonable

PASS 7 of 7 checks hold and every declared subsystem was exercised
